/-!
# The order of vanishing of a local equation is the multiplicity of the subscheme it cuts out

Let `Y` be a locally Noetherian integral scheme, let `Z ⊆ Y` be a closed subscheme and let `ξ` be
a point of codimension one at which the ideal of `Z` is generated by the germ of a section `t`
defined on an open `V ∋ ξ`. Then the order of vanishing at `ξ` of the rational function that `t`
represents is the multiplicity of `Z` at `ξ`:

  `ord_ξ(t) = length_{𝒪_{Y,ξ}}(𝒪_{Z,ξ})`.

Both sides are lengths of the same module. The left side is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ord`,
which at a codimension-one point is `Ring.ordFrac` of the local ring and hence, on an element of
the local ring itself, the length of the quotient by the principal ideal it generates. The right
side is `Stacks.Chow.componentMultiplicity`, the length of the stalk of `Z`, and the stalk of `Z`
is the quotient of the stalk of `Y` by the stalk of the ideal sheaf of `Z`. So the content is the
hypothesis that those two ideals of `𝒪_{Y,ξ}` agree, which is what "`t` is a local equation for
`Z` at `ξ`" says.

The use of this is to read off a coefficient of the cycle of a closed subscheme. The cycle
`[Z]_{n-1}` is indexed by the generic points of the components of `Z`, so its coefficient at a
codimension-one point of `Y` is only available after that point has been recognised as such a
generic point; on an integral `Y` of delta-dimension `n` whose generic point avoids `Z`, that
recognition is `Stacks.Chow.exists_genericPoints_of_coheight_one`. Combining the two gives the
coefficientwise comparison `ord_ξ(t) = [Z]_{n-1}(ξ)` of a principal divisor with the cycle of the
closed subscheme its local equations cut out.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.ord_eq_ringOrd_germ`: the order of vanishing of the rational function represented
  by a section is the order of vanishing, in the sense of `Ring.ord`, of its germ.
* `Stacks.Chow.ord_eq_componentMultiplicity`: the order of vanishing of a local equation for `Z`
  at a codimension-one point is the multiplicity of `Z` there.
* `Stacks.Chow.exists_germ_span_eq_stalk_of_isLocallyPrincipal`: a locally principal closed
  subscheme missing the generic point has a nonzero local equation at every point, which is the
  hypothesis the previous statement takes.
* `Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply_eq_zero_of_notMem_range`: outside `Z` the
  cycle of `Z` has coefficient zero.
* `Stacks.Chow.principalDivisorCycle_apply_eq_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply`: the
  coefficientwise comparison, at a codimension-one point of `Z`, of the principal divisor of a
  local equation with the cycle of `Z`.

## Implementation notes

The passage from `Ring.ord` to the multiplicity goes through the stalk of the ideal sheaf,
`AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk`, in two steps that are each an identity of lengths of
one module: `Ring.ord R x` is by definition `Module.length R (R ⧸ Ideal.span {x})`, so the local
equation hypothesis turns it into the length of `𝒪_{Y,ξ}` modulo the stalk of the ideal sheaf;
and that quotient is the stalk of `Z`, which is the content of
`Stacks.Blowup.Colength.length_idealStalk_quotient_eq_subschemeStalk`. No affine open is chosen
here — both inputs are already stated at the stalk.

The side conditions are mild and all follow from `t ≠ 0`: the germ of a nonzero section at a
point of an integral scheme is nonzero (`AlgebraicGeometry.germ_injective_of_isIntegral`), the
local ring is a domain, so the germ is a nonzerodivisor, and the length is then finite because
the local ring is Noetherian of dimension at most one
(`Ring.ord_ne_top`). Finiteness is what lets the `ℕ∞`-valued `Ring.ord` be compared with the
`ℤ`-valued order of vanishing.

`Stacks.Chow.principalDivisorCycle_apply_eq_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply` carries
`[IsLocallyNoetherian Y]` as an instance argument although it follows from
`LocallyOfFiniteType p`; this matches `Stacks.Chow.principalDivisorCycle_apply`, whose right-hand
side `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ord` is stated under that instance.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02MD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02QU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02QU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02RO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02RO)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Order TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-- The germ of a nonzero section on a nonempty open of an integral scheme is nonzero. -/
private theorem germ_hom_ne_zero {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y] {V : Y.Opens} [Nonempty V]
    {ξ : Y} (hξV : ξ ∈ V) {t : Γ(Y, V)} (ht : t ≠ 0) : (Y.presheaf.germ V ξ hξV).hom t ≠ 0 :=
  fun h => ht (germ_injective_of_isIntegral Y ξ hξV (by simpa using h))

/-- The order of vanishing at a codimension-one point of the rational function represented by a
section `t` on an open neighbourhood is the order of vanishing, in the sense of `Ring.ord`, of
the germ of `t` in the local ring. -/
theorem ord_eq_ringOrd_germ {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    {ξ : Y} (hco : coheight ξ = 1)
    {V : Y.Opens} [Nonempty V] (hξV : ξ ∈ V) (t : Γ(Y, V)) (ht : t ≠ 0)
    {n : ℕ} (hn : Ring.ord (Y.presheaf.stalk ξ) ((Y.presheaf.germ V ξ hξV).hom t) = n) :
    Y.ord (Y.germToFunctionField V t) ξ = n := by
  have : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 (Y.presheaf.stalk ξ) := krullDimLE_of_coheight_le hco.le
  have hgerm := germ_hom_ne_zero hξV ht
  have hff : Y.germToFunctionField V t ≠ 0 := fun h =>
    ht (Scheme.germToFunctionField_injective Y V (by simpa using h))
  rw [Scheme.ord_eq_iff hco hff]
  change (Ring.ordFrac (Y.presheaf.stalk ξ)) _ = _
  rw [← Scheme.algebraMap_germ_eq_germToFunctionField Y hξV t,
    Ring.ordFrac_eq_ord _ hgerm,
    Ring.ordMonoidWithZeroHom_eq_coe _ (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hgerm) hn]

/-- The order of vanishing at a codimension-one point of a local equation for a closed subscheme
`Z` is the multiplicity of `Z` at that point.

The hypothesis `hZt` is that the stalk of the ideal sheaf of `Z` at the point is generated by
the germ of `t`, which is what it means for `t` to be a local equation for `Z` there. -/
theorem ord_eq_componentMultiplicity {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    (Z : Y.IdealSheafData) (ξ : genericPoints Z.subscheme)
    (hco : coheight (Z.subschemeι ξ.1) = 1)
    {V : Y.Opens} [Nonempty V] (hξV : Z.subschemeι ξ.1 ∈ V) (t : Γ(Y, V)) (ht : t ≠ 0)
    (hZt : IdealSheafData.stalk Z (Z.subschemeι ξ.1) =
      Ideal.span {(Y.presheaf.germ V (Z.subschemeι ξ.1) hξV).hom t}) :
    Y.ord (Y.germToFunctionField V t) (Z.subschemeι ξ.1) =
      componentMultiplicity Z.subschemeι ξ := by
  have : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 (Y.presheaf.stalk (Z.subschemeι ξ.1)) :=
    krullDimLE_of_coheight_le hco.le
  have hgerm := germ_hom_ne_zero hξV ht
  have htop : Ring.ord (Y.presheaf.stalk (Z.subschemeι ξ.1))
      ((Y.presheaf.germ V (Z.subschemeι ξ.1) hξV).hom t) ≠ ⊤ :=
    Ring.ord_ne_top (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hgerm)
  have hlen : Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk (Z.subschemeι ξ.1))
      (Y.presheaf.stalk (Z.subschemeι ξ.1) ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk Z (Z.subschemeι ξ.1)) =
      Ring.ord (Y.presheaf.stalk (Z.subschemeι ξ.1))
        ((Y.presheaf.germ V (Z.subschemeι ξ.1) hξV).hom t) := by
    rw [hZt]; rfl
  rw [componentMultiplicity_eq_length_stalk,
    ← Stacks.Blowup.Colength.length_idealStalk_quotient_eq_subschemeStalk Z ξ.1, hlen,
    ord_eq_ringOrd_germ hco hξV t ht (ENat.natCast_toNat htop).symm]

/-- A locally principal closed subscheme of an irreducible scheme whose generic point it misses
has, at every point, a *nonzero* local equation on an affine open neighbourhood: a section
generating the stalk of its ideal sheaf there.

This is the hypothesis `Stacks.Chow.ord_eq_componentMultiplicity` takes, obtained from local
principality in the sense of Tag 01WR. Nonvanishing of the generator is where the generic point
is used: a generator that vanished would make the ideal sheaf zero on the whole neighbourhood,
putting the generic point into the support. -/
theorem exists_germ_span_eq_stalk_of_isLocallyPrincipal {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace Y]
    (I : Y.IdealSheafData) (hI : Stacks.Divisors.IsLocallyPrincipal I)
    (hgen : genericPoint Y ∉ (I.support : Set Y)) (x : Y) :
    ∃ (U : Y.affineOpens) (hx : x ∈ (U : Set Y)) (t : Γ(Y, U)), t ≠ 0 ∧
      IdealSheafData.stalk I x =
        Ideal.span {(Y.presheaf.germ (U : Y.Opens) x hx).hom t} := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, ⟨t, hspan⟩⟩ := hI x
  refine ⟨U, hxU, t, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro h0
    have hηU : genericPoint Y ∈ (U : Set Y) :=
      ((genericPoint_spec Y).mem_open_set_iff (U : Y.Opens).2).mpr (by simpa using ⟨x, hxU⟩)
    refine hgen ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem hηU).mpr ?_)
    rw [hspan, Scheme.zeroLocus_span, h0]
    simp
  · rw [IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ I x U hxU, hspan, Ideal.map_span]
    simp

/-- The cycle of a closed subscheme has coefficient zero at a point outside the subscheme: its
coefficients are supported on the images of the generic points of the components. -/
theorem cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply_eq_zero_of_notMem_range (C : ChowSituation.{u})
    {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (p : Y ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p] (i : Z ⟶ Y)
    [IsClosedImmersion i] (k : ℤ) {x : Y} (hx : x ∉ Set.range i.base) :
    (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p i k).1 x = 0 :=
  cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply_eq_zero C p i k x
    fun ⟨ξ, hξ, _⟩ => hx ⟨ξ.1, hξ⟩

/-- At a codimension-one point of a closed subscheme `Z` of an integral scheme `Y` of
delta-dimension `n` whose generic point avoids `Z`, the principal divisor of a local equation for
`Z` and the cycle `[Z]_{n-1}` have the same coefficient.

This is the coefficientwise comparison of a principal divisor with the cycle of the closed
subscheme its local equations cut out. The point is recognised as the generic point of a
component of `Z` of delta-dimension `n - 1` by
`Stacks.Chow.exists_genericPoints_of_coheight_one`, which is what makes the coefficient of
`[Z]_{n-1}` readable there. -/
@[ega "IV 21.6.7" "special case"]
theorem principalDivisorCycle_apply_eq_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply
    (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {Y : Scheme.{u}} (p : Y ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] {n : ℤ}
    (hn : schemeDeltaDimension C p = (n : EInt)) (Z : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (hgen : genericPoint Y ∉ Set.range Z.subschemeι.base)
    {ξ : Y} (hco : coheight ξ = 1) (hξZ : ξ ∈ Set.range Z.subschemeι.base)
    {V : Y.Opens} [Nonempty V] (hξV : ξ ∈ V) (t : Γ(Y, V)) (ht : t ≠ 0)
    (hZt : IdealSheafData.stalk Z ξ = Ideal.span {(Y.presheaf.germ V ξ hξV).hom t}) :
    (principalDivisorCycle C p hn (Y.germToFunctionField V t) : AlgebraicCycle Y ℤ) ξ =
      (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p Z.subschemeι (n - 1)).1 ξ := by
  obtain ⟨η, hη, hδ⟩ :=
    exists_genericPoints_of_coheight_one C p Z.subschemeι hn hgen hco hξZ
  subst hη
  rw [principalDivisorCycle_apply,
    cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply C p Z.subschemeι (n - 1) η hδ,
    ord_eq_componentMultiplicity Z η hco hξV t ht hZt]

end Stacks.Chow

end
